# Vendored Wayland shell protocol definitions (interface XML only).
#
# Consumed by the wayland-cxx-scanner (wcs) at build time to generate the client bindings
# for the non-standard shells acl targets via ACL_WL_SHELL (agl / ivi / simple). The stable
# desktop shells (xdg-shell, presentation-time, viewporter, fractional-scale, linux-dmabuf,
# text-input-v3) come from the system `wayland-protocols` package and are NOT vendored here;
# only protocols absent from that package are vendored.
#
# These are unmodified upstream interface definitions. No implementation code is vendored.
# All three are MIT-licensed (permitted; see PROVENANCE.md). No GPL-3.0 sources.

name: "wayland-protocols (vendored shell subset)"
description: "agl_shell, ivi_application, and zwp_fullscreen_shell_v1 protocol XML for wcs codegen."

